## Key Findings Summary

| Severity | Count | Key Items |
|----------|-------|-----------|
| High | 1 | ResStock `from_resstock()` hardcodes 24-hour simulation — silently truncates annual energy analysis to 1 day (`fleet.rs:549`) |
| Medium | 3 | Fleet deep-cloned per `simulate()` call to attach progress callback; no explicit `shutdown()`/`cleanup()` (relies on Drop); doc references deprecated `Python::with_gil` |
| Low | 5 | Panic path skips progress callback invocation; aggregate timeseries uses UTF-8 timestamps instead of native Arrow type; `SteppableFleet` culls heterogeneous-timing dwellings; sequential dwelling build; per-dwelling metrics lack `bldg_id` column |

## GIL Safety Assessment

The GIL management is **correct**: `py.detach(|| ...)` releases the GIL before Rayon parallel execution, and `Python::attach(|py| { ... })` in the progress callback reacquires it per worker thread. The `Py<PyAny>` callback reference is properly `Send + Sync`. No GIL corruption or deadlock risks were identified.

## Heterogeneity

`Fleet::simulate()` supports heterogeneous dwellings (different HPXML files, different durations) without restriction. `SteppableFleet` requires homogeneous timing — dwellings with different `total_steps` or `time_res` are silently culled at construction time (`fleet.rs:341-368`).
